    "C": "Private encoder owns the cache; each project invocation creates two separate factory instances for sprite and tile. Catalog/source remain case-local and no global persistent cache or product changes.",
    "D": "Two actual callers share encode+gzip+digest and failure/lifetime contract. Fixed frame factories differ, so no boolean mode/universal asset service or copied algorithms.",
    "E": "Nine identities, bodies, assertions and timeouts AST-identical; all pass. Separate private complete-input and cache ownership/error probes do not count as new gameplay tests or business mutation counters.",
    "F": "frame-count and frame factory make reuse key/representation explicit; project and rendering stages remain readable, no generic invocation context.",
    "G": "563 per-case resource encodings reduce to 15 by removing repeated work; redundant per-loop Uint8Array.from removed only after helper guarantees owned copies. No test retirement/dead-code restoration.",
    "H": "Pure fixture preparation is isolated and directly probed for buffer independence, kind/factory separation and failed-entry retry; real serving/escort/normal input contract still runs unmocked."
  },
